{
  "_readme": [
    "Maps each real photo to the temporary (stock) photo it replaces.",
    "Photos live in public/images/. Naming: team photos = team-carlos-NN-<what>.jpg;",
    "job photos = recent-projects/<job-type>-<location>/<before|during|after>-<subject>.jpg (no year when unknown).",
    "Fill a slot by putting the new filename in its 'file' field, then run:",
    "  node scripts/sync-images.mjs            (dry run: shows what would happen)",
    "  node scripts/sync-images.mjs --apply    (uploads to Firebase Storage + updates the code)",
    "Never use a filename that already exists in Storage: Storage files are cached for a year.",
    "'galleryOnly' lists photos used in lib/gallery-data.ts; the script uploads them too.",
    "Redesign (Oct 31 2026): photos committed under public/images/recent-projects/, public/images/2026-waterproofing-nwdc/ and team-carlos-04+ are served straight from the site (lib/sample-photos.ts isCommittedPhoto), so the Firebase upload is optional for them.",
    "The redesigned homepage no longer uses Hero.tsx or MeetCarlos.tsx; its photos (hero, featured projects, before/after, service cards) are set in lib/site-images.ts.",
    "Slots still empty show a sample photo until filled (lib/sample-photos.ts, USE_SAMPLE_PHOTOS)."
